## Intuition
// Intuition behind the code:

// 1. The pattern is symmetric: it has an upper half and a lower half.
//    - Upper half: stars increase on both sides, spaces decrease in the middle.
//    - Lower half: stars decrease on both sides, spaces increase in the middle.

// 2. First loop (upper half):
//    - Loop variable i goes from 1 to n.
//    - Left stars: print i stars.
//    - Middle spaces: print 2*(n-i) spaces.
//    - Right stars: print i stars.
//    - This creates growing stars with shrinking spaces.

// 3. Second loop (lower half):
//    - Loop variable i goes from 1 to n-1.
//    - Left stars: print (n-i) stars.
//    - Middle spaces: print 2*i spaces.
//    - Right stars: print (n-i) stars.
//    - This creates shrinking stars with growing spaces.

// 4. Together, both loops form a symmetric hourglass / double triangle pattern.



## Approach

// The pattern is divided into two symmetric halves.
// In the upper half, the number of stars increases on both sides while the spaces in the middle decrease.
// For each row i (1 to n), we print i stars, then 2*(n-i) spaces, then i stars again.
// In the lower half, the number of stars decreases on both sides while the spaces in the middle increase.
// For each row i (1 to n-1), we print (n-i) stars, then 2*i spaces, then (n-i) stars again.
// This ensures symmetry and produces the hourglass/double triangle pattern.
// Time Complexity: O(n^2) since we print about n characters for each of 2n rows.
// Space Complexity: O(1) as no extra data structures are used.


